From: OpenWrt cake-autorate build <local>
Subject: [PATCH] speedtest-go: never block in AccompanyEcho.Stop

Stop() sends on an unbuffered channel. When the echo goroutine has
already returned (no connection, early error) nobody receives and Stop()
blocks for the rest of the process lifetime; cake-autorate-rs then has
to kill the backend on its timeout. A buffer of one lets Stop() return
whether or not the goroutine is still there; the goroutine still sees the
value when it is.

--- a/speedtest.go
+++ b/speedtest.go
@@ -258,7 +258,7 @@
 	return &AccompanyEcho{
 		server:   server,
 		interval: interval,
-		stopEcho: make(chan bool),
+		stopEcho: make(chan bool, 1),
 	}
 }
 
